Z||000000||jch82||04-05-2001||11:29 PM||||When I'm cruising about 60mph and swerve back and forth a little bit (sounds bad but you know what i mean), the back end is pretty jumpy....My grandpa and uncle both say it is struts and I was wondering how hard these are to replace? Should I do it myself or have a specialist do it? Thanks<P>Josh  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Yeah, my girlfriend takes collect calls from the road<BR>And it doesn't seem to matter that I'm lacking in the bulge<BR>She laughs at my dumb jokes when no one does<BR>She brings me mexican food from Sombrero's just because<BR>                 <I>-Blink 182</I>||||reg||5
Z||000001||rogergarrison||04-06-2001||12:33 AM||||bounce the rear of the car up and down hard a few times and see if it stops immediatly when you stop. If it does there OK, and you have problems with alignment, bushings or cradle. There not that big a deal to replace, but you have to have it aligned after anyway, so Id just let them put them on.||||reg||1
